    {
      "sourceFile": "MakingScreens.swift",
      "line": 4,
      "texts": [
        "Measure six equal lengths of cotton cord. Cut carefully, leaving extra length for the fringe.",
        "Place your dowel on a flat surface. Mark evenly spaced positions for each cord.",
        "Fold a cord in half, place the loop over the dowel, and pull the ends through. Repeat across the row.",
        "Work across the row, keeping the knots evenly spaced. Add texture with the wool yarn.",
        "Comb out the fringe and trim it slowly to your preferred shape.",
        "Attach a hanging cord, check that the dowel is balanced, and hang your finished weave."
      ]
    },
